    {
      "id": "claim_08f2ee8ddc0943ebaa47a7410ecda3fd",
      "statement": "PATCH /api/tasks/:taskId with { action: 'stop' } is the only writer of status='stopped' and only succeeds when existingTask.status === 'processing' (else 400 'Task can only be stopped when it is in progress'). On success it writes status='stopped', error='Task was stopped by user', completedAt=now, updatedAt=now, and calls killSandbox(taskId) which removes the entry from the in-memory Map and calls sandbox.stop() (best-effort; SDK errors are swallowed). killSandbox falls back to killing the oldest registered sandbox if no entry exists for the taskId — a 'Try Again' fallback. After the worker has finished and the registry is empty, the DB flip to status='stopped' is the only effect; the SDK timeout bounds the VM.",
      "evidence": [
