    {
      "id": "claim_41551c041921473c9013ed1a30cdaac7",
      "statement": "POST /api/tasks/:taskId/start-sandbox rejects with 400 'Keep-alive is not enabled for this task' when task.keepAlive is false; when keepAlive=true it probes any existing sandboxId/sandboxUrl via Sandbox.get + runCommandInSandbox('echo', ['test']), returning 400 'Sandbox is already running' on success or clearing the DB columns and falling through to a fresh Sandbox.create({ source: { type: 'git', url: task.repoUrl, revision: task.branchName, depth: 1 }, timeout: maxDurationMinutes * 60_000, ports: [port], runtime: 'node22', resources: { vcpus: 4 } }) on failure. The route configures git, installs Node/Python dependencies, starts the dev server in detached mode with [SERVER] log capture, and persists sandboxId/sandboxUrl back to the row.",
