    {
      "id": "claim_5785ad04faec42eeb3b0510899a0c861",
      "statement": "POST /api/tasks/:taskId/stop-sandbox is the only endpoint outside the worker that calls sandbox.stop() on the SDK directly. It rejects with 400 'Sandbox is not active' if task.sandboxId is null, reconnects via Sandbox.get(sandboxId), calls sandbox.stop(), unregisterSandbox(taskId), and writes sandboxId=NULL, sandboxUrl=NULL. The keepAlive flag is not consulted — an explicit stop tears the VM down regardless of the original task opt-in. The task status is left as-is; only the two pointer columns change.",
      "evidence": [
