    {
      "id": "claim_46fc2a5a93a149018f267f3ec8dd2d95",
      "statement": "The four follow-up routes have distinct row-state effects: continue rewinds any non-pending row to status='processing' + completedAt=NULL; start-sandbox leaves status untouched and creates/registers a sandbox; stop-sandbox clears sandboxId+sandboxUrl but not status; PATCH action=stop flips to status='stopped', error='Task was stopped by user', completedAt=now, and only fires when the row is currently processing. Only continue touches the daily rate-limit counter; the other three do not insert taskMessages rows.",
